  "transcript": {
    "text": "The most dangerous person in the world is the person who is not scared of being alone. You can't control someone who's okay with being alone. You can't threaten to leave them. You can't pressure them into a bad deal. You can't make them fall for a fake friendship. They are simply not scared of walking away. Some people are terrified of being alone, and because of that they end up tolerating a bunch of shit. But the moment you're actually fine with being alone, nobody can use that fear against you. That is real freedom.",
